@page
@model BeeMemoryBank.Web.Pages.Admin.MasterPasswordModel

@section About {
    <p>
        The master password is the one secret that opens this node's copy of the vault key. Everything in the vault is encrypted under that key; the password never
        leaves the node, and only a key derived from it is used to unwrap the vault key (so it cannot be recovered if you forget it; for that you need a
        <a href="/Admin/RecoveryKey">recovery key</a>).
    </p>
    <p>
        <strong>Changing it changes this node only.</strong> Each node keeps its own wrapped copy of the vault key, and those are never synced and are stripped from join
        packages. So every other node keeps accepting the <em>old</em> password, including at its own join endpoint, which is what lets a new node become a full member of
        the network. The other nodes are told that the password changed, but no key material crosses the wire, so a person has to type the new password on each of them.
        Until you do, the page of that node warns about it.
    </p>
    <p>
        A password change does <strong>not</strong> throw out a node or an agent that already holds the vault key. To lock one out you have to revoke it
        (<a href="/Admin/Devices">Devices</a>, <a href="/Admin/Agents">Agents</a>) and <a href="/Admin/DekRotation">rotate the data key</a>.
    </p>
}

<partial name="_MasterPasswordNotice" model="Model" />

<div class="card mt-md" style="max-width:560px;">
    <form method="post" asp-page-handler="ChangeMasterPassword" data-busy="long" data-busy-title="Changing the master password" style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:12px;">
        <sl-input name="oldPassword" type="password" password-toggle autocomplete="off"
                  data-1p-ignore data-lpignore="true" required
                  label="Current master password"></sl-input>
        <sl-input name="newPassword" type="password" password-toggle autocomplete="off"
                  data-1p-ignore data-lpignore="true" required
                  label="New master password"></sl-input>
        <p class="text-muted text-sm" style="margin:0;" id="master-password-hint-intro">
            Password hint (required). If you forget your password, we will show this hint on the sign-in page,
            because there is no e-mail recovery. Write it so that other people cannot work out your password
            from it. Never write the password itself. Anyone who can read this node's data folder can read the hint, so never write anything secret in it.
        </p>
        <sl-input name="passwordHint" autocomplete="off" required maxlength="120"
                  data-1p-ignore data-lpignore="true"
                  label="Password hint" help-text="1 to 120 characters."></sl-input>
        <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;">
            <sl-button type="submit" variant="warning" class="btn-confirm-click"
                data-confirm="Change the master password on THIS node? Other nodes keep accepting the old one until you change it there too.">
                <sl-icon slot="prefix" name="key"></sl-icon> Change master password
            </sl-button>
            <span class="text-muted text-sm" data-busy-note hidden role="status">Changing the master password...</span>
        </div>
    </form>
</div>
